sited. Add Montserrat and Core.\n\nQueue: [Eileen, Oliver, Montserrat, Core]\n\nVisited: Shae, Rees, Aliza, R, Caro, Yitz, Eileen, Oliver, Montserrat, Core\n\nDequeue Eileen, check its neighbors: Aliza, R, Caro.\n\nAll visited. Nothing new.\n\nQueue: [Oliver, Montserrat, Core]\n\nDequeue Oliver, check its neighbors: Caro.\n\nCaro is visited. So nothing new.\n\nBut we're looking for Oliver, so we've reached him at level 2.\n\nWait, no. Wait, Shae is at level 0. Rees, Aliza, R are level 1. Then Caro, Yitz, Eileen are level 2. Then from Yitz, we add Mont and Core, which are level 3. Then from Core, we can reach Jo, which is level 4. But we're looking for Oliver, who is at level 2.\n\nWait, no. Let me retrace.\n\nWait, when we dequeued Caro at level 2, its neighbor is Olivers, so Oliver is added at level 3.\n\nWait, no. Let me correct.\n\nWait, when we process Caro (from Rees at level 1), Caro's neighbors are Rees, Olivers, Aliza. Rees and Aliza are visited, so we add Olivers at level 2.\n\nSo when we process Caro, we add Olivers to level 2.\n\nThen, when we process Yitz at level 2, we add Mont and Core at level 3.\n\nThen, when we process Eileen at level 2, we add nothing new.\n\nThen, when we process Oliver at level 2, we check its neighbors, which is Caro, already visited.\n\nSo the shortest path from Shae to Oliver is through Rees -> Caro -> Oliver, which is two steps, so level 2.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's a shorter path.\n\nAlternatively, Shae is connected to R (Aliza's friend), and R is connected to Eileen, who is connected to Caro, who is connected to Oliver. So that's Shae -> R -> Eileen -> Caro -> Oliver, which is four steps, which is longer.\n\nAlternatively, Shae -> Rees -> Yitz -> Core -> Jo -> Ed -> Mont -> Yitz? No, that's not helpful.\n\nWait, perhaps I'm getting confused. Let me list the BFS steps properly.\n\nLevel 0: Shae\n\nLevel 1: Rees, Aliza, R\n\nLevel 2: From Rees: Caro, Yitz\n\nFrom Aliza: Eileen\n\nFrom R: Eileen\n\nSo after level 2,