  [105/1150] '<think>\nAlright, let\'s tackle this problem step by step. So, the question is about finding the shortest path for Edens\' message to reach Shawn using the given friendship graph. The options are whether she should pass the message to Montserrat or Oliver first. \n\nFirst, I need to visualize the graph based on the provided friendships. I\'ll list out all the connections to understand how each person is linked. \n\nStarting with Edens, she\'s friends with Montserrat and Oliver. So, from Edens, the first step can be either Montserrat or Oliver. \n\nLooking at Montserrat, her friends are Yitzchak and Edens. Yitzchak is also connected to Core, Rochel, and Montserrat. From Yitzchak, we can reach Core, which is connected to Rochel, and so on. But I\'m looking for a path to Shawn, so I need to see if there\'s a connection from Montserrat to someone who knows someone who knows Shawn.\n\nNow, looking at Olivers\' friends: he\'s connected to Caroleen, Eileen, and Edens. Eileen is friends with Aliza and Caroleen. Aliza is connected to Rees, Yitzchak, and Eileen. Rees is friends with Caroleen and Edens. Caroleen is also connected to Aliza. So, from Olivers, we can go to Eileen, then to Aliza, then to Rees, and then to Caroleen, and finally to Shown. \n\nWait, but is there a shorter path? Let me check if there\'s a connection from Olivers to someone who can reach Shown quicker. Shown is directly connected to Rees and Caroleen. Rees is connected to Edens and Caroleen. Caroleen is connected to Aliza and Edens. Aliza is connected to Eileen and Yitzchak. Eileen is connected to Aliza and Caroleen. Yitzchak is connected to Core, Montserrat, and Edens. Core is connected to Rochel and Edens. Rochel is connected to Core and Yitzchak. \n\nWait, maybe there\'s a shorter path through Yitzchak. Let me see: Edens -> Yitzchak -> Core -> Rochel -> Shown. That\'s four steps. Alternatively, Edens -> Yitzchak -> Core -> Rees -> Shown. That\'s also four steps. \n\nBut wait, is there 