er connections.\n\nWait, let's check if there's a direct connection from Yitta to Vanessa. From the data, Yitta is friends with Colette and Empress. Empress is friends with Vanessa. So Yitta to Empress to Vanessa is two steps. Alternatively, Yitta to Colette, Colette to Empress, then Empress to Vanessa. That's three steps. So the direct path through Empress is shorter.\n\nWait, but maybe there's another way. Let me check all connections again. Yitta is friends with Colette and Empress. Empress is friends with Vanessa. So Yitta to Empress is one step, then Empress to Vanessa is another. So the path is Yitta -> Empress -> Vanessa. That's two steps.\n\nAlternatively, Yitta to Colette, Colette to Empress, then Empress to Vanessa. That's three steps. So the direct path through Empress is shorter.\n\nWait, but in the initial data, Yitta is friends with Empress, so that's a direct connection. So the shortest path is Yitta -> Empress -> Vanessa. So Yitta should pass to Empress first.\n\nWait, but in the initial question, the options are to pass to Empress or Colette. So the shortest path is two steps via Empress, whereas via Colette it's three steps. So Yitta should pass to Empress.\n\nWait, but let me make sure. Let me list all possible paths from Yitta to Vanessa.\n\n1. Yitta -> Empress -> Vanessa (two steps)\n2. Yitta -> Colette -> Empress -> Vanessa (three steps)\n3. Yitta -> Colette -> Theodor -> Yitta -> Empress -> Vanessa (loops, so not efficient)\n4. Yitta -> Colette -> Russell -> Vanes (but Vanes is not connected to Vanessa)\nWait, Vanes is connected to Russell and Kait. Kait is connected to Nevaeh and Kai. Nevaeh is connected to Kait, Theodor, and Colette. Theodor is connected to Yitta and Colette. So no direct connection from Vanes to Vanessa.\n\nSo the only direct connection is through Empress. So the shortest path is Yitta -> Empress -> Vanessa. Therefore, Yitta should pass to Empress.\n</think>\n\nyitta -> empress -> vanessa empress"  correct=empress
