  [204/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Theodore should pass the message to Christina or Yitta to get to Toby the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll apply that here.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Theodore is connected to Yitta and Colette. From there, I'll explore each option.\n\nIf he goes to Yitta first, Yitta is connected to Colette and Emress. Colette is also connected to Yitta, Emress, and Russell. Emress is connected to Vanessas. Vanessas are connected to Russell and Faiga. Faiga is connected to Nevaeh and Tiff. Tiff is connected to Kait, Katherine, and Faiga. Kait is connected to Nevaeh and Toby. So from Yitta, the path to Toby would be Yitta -> Colette -> Emress -> Vanessas -> Russell -> Vanessas -> Nevaeh -> Kait -> Toby. That's 8 steps.\n\nAlternatively, if he goes to Colette first, Colette is connected to Yitta, Emress, Russell, and Theod. From Colette, Emress is connected to Vanessas, who connect to Russell and Faiga. Russell is connected to Vanessas and Colette. Colette is connected to Yitta and Emress. Yitta is connected to Emress and Colette. So the path would be Theodore -> Colette -> Emress -> Vanessas -> Russell -> Vanessas -> Nevaeh -> Kait -> Toby. That's also 8 steps.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path. Let me check again. From Colette, she's connected to Emress and Yitta. Emress is connected to Vanessas, who connect to Russell and Faiga. Russell is connected to Vanessas and Colette. So from Colette, the path could be Theodore -> Colette -> Emress -> Vanessas -> Russell -> Vanessas -> Nevaeh -> Kait -> Toby. That's still 8 steps.\n\nHmm, maybe I'm missing a shorter path. Let me see if there's a way through Yitta. From Yitta, she's connected to Colette and Emress. Colette is connected to Emress and Yitta. So maybe from Yitta, the path is Theodore -> Yitta -> Emress -> Vanessas -> Russell -> Vanessas -> Nevaeh -> Kait -> Toby. That's also 8 ste