  [319/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Esteban should pass the message to Freida or Ibrahim to get it to Bruchy the most efficiently. I'll use BFS for this, which means I'll explore all possible paths layer by layer.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Esteban is friends with Freida, Ibrahim, and Rebecca. So from Esteban, the first step is to his friends: Freida, Ibrahim, Rebecca.\n\nLooking at Freida's friends: She's connected to Rebecca, Tehila, and maybe others. But since we're starting from Esteban, Freida's friends are already at distance 1 from Esteban.\n\nIbrahim's friends: He's connected to Esteban, Aibrahim, and maybe others. So Ibrahim is also at distance 1.\n\nNow, looking at Bruchy. Bruchy is friends with Aissatou and Nicolle. Aissatou is connected to Bruchy and Alessandra. Alessandra is connected to Aissatou and Eyad. Eyad is connected to Alessandra and Egypt. Egypt is connected to Eyad and Bruchy. So Bruchy is two steps away from Aissatou, which is connected to Alessandra, and so on.\n\nWait, but Bruchy is also connected to Nicolle, who is connected to Egypt, which is connected to Eyad, and so on. So Bruchy is two steps away from Egypt, which is connected to Eyad, but that's a longer path.\n\nAlternatively, looking back, Bruchy is connected to Aissatou, who is connected to Alessandra, who is connected to Eyad, who is connected to Egypt, who is connected to Bruchy. That's a longer path.\n\nBut wait, maybe there's a shorter path through other friends. Let me check if Bruchy is connected directly to anyone else. From the data, Bruchy is friends with Aissatou and Nicolle. So Bruchy is two steps away from Aissatou and Nicolle.\n\nBut looking at the connections, Bruchy is not directly connected to Freida or Ibrahim. So the message needs to go through friends of friends.\n\nSo from Esteban, the first step is to Freida, Ibrahim, or Rebecca. If he goes to Freida, then Freida is connected to Rebecca, Tehila, etc. If he goes to Ibrahim, then Ibrahim is connected to Aibrahim and others.\n\nBut Bruchy is not directly connected to Freida or Ibrahim. So the next step would be to see if any of Freida's or Ibrahim's friends are connected to Bruchy.\n\nLooking at Freida's friends: She's connected to Rebecca, Tehila, and maybe others. But Bruchy isn't directly connected to Freida. So from Freida, the next step would be to her friends, but none of them are Bruchy.\n\nSimilarly, from Ibrahim, his friends are Aibrahim and maybe others. Bruchy isn't directly connected to Ibrahim either.\n\nWait, but maybe through another layer. So from Esteban to Freida, then Freida to her friends, but none are Bruchy. So the next step would be to go to the next layer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe through Rebecca. Esteban is connected to Rebecca, and Rebecca is connected to Freida and Dashiell. Dashiell is connected to Morris and Rebecca. Morris is connected to Tehila and Dashiell. Tehila is connected to Freida and Morris. So from Esteban to Rebecca to Dashiell to Morris to Tehila to Freida. But that's a longer path.\n\nWait, but the question is about the shortest path. So maybe there's a shorter path through another route.\n\nWait, looking back, Bruchy is connected to Aissatou and Nicolle. Aissatou is connected to Alessandra, who is connected to Eyad, who is connected to Egypt, who is connected to Bruchy. So that's a path from Bruchy to Egypt to Eyad to Alessandra to Aissatou. But that's from Bruchy's side.\n\nAlternatively, maybe from Esteban to Freida to Rebecca to Dashiell to Morris to Tehila to Freida again, but that's looping, which BFS avoids.\n\nWait, maybe I'm overcomplicating. Let me try to map the BFS layers.\n\nStarting from Esteban:\n\nLayer 0: Esteban\n\nLayer 1: Freida, Ibrahim, Rebecca\n\nLayer 2: From Freida: Rebecc, Tehila, maybe others. From Ibrahim: Aibrahim, maybe others. From Rebecca: Freida, Dashiell.\n\nSo in layer 2, we have Rebecc, Tehila, Aibrahim, Dashiell.\n\nNow, check if any of these are Bruchy. No