 shorter path through another route. Let me see. From Emery, Seth is friends with Maimouna. So that's one step. So the path is Eyad -> Emery -> Seth -> Maimouna, which is three steps. Alternatively, through Hafsa, it's four steps. So the shortest path is through Emery.\n\nWait, but I'm getting confused. Let me try to visualize the graph.\n\nEyad is connected to Hafsa and Emery.\n\nHafsa is connected to Eya and Fanta (from the given data, Hafsa is friends with Fanta). Eya is connected to Emery.\n\nEmery is connected to Seth and Aimee.\n\nSeth is connected to Maimouna and Eya.\n\nSo from Eyad, going to Hafsa:\n\nHafsa -> Eya -> Emery -> Seth -> Maimouna. That's four steps.\n\nFrom Eyad, going to Emery:\n\nEmery -> Seth -> Maimouna. That's three steps.\n\nSo the shortest path is through Emery, which is three steps. Therefore, Eyad should pass the message to Emery first.\n</think>\n\neyad -> emery -> seth -> maimouna\n\nemery"  correct=emery
