  [407/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Emery should pass the message to Eyad or Aimee to get to Fanta the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll apply that here.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Emery is connected to Aimee and Eyad. Aimee is connected to Emery, Maimouna, Abdul, and Seth. Eyad is connected to Emery, Aimee, and Hafsa. \n\nFrom Emery, the first step is to look at all direct friends. So, Aimee and Eyad are both at distance 1. \n\nLooking at Aimee's friends, she's connected to Maimouna, Abdul, and Seth. Maimouna is friends with Pedro and Aimee, so Pedro is at distance 2. Abdul is friends with Pedro and Aimee, so Pedro is also connected through Abdul. Seth is connected to Aimee, Emery, and Hafsa. Hafsa is friends with Emery, Fanta, and Prince. \n\nWait, Hafsa is connected to Fanta, so if we go through Hafsa, that's two steps from Emery: Emery -> Eyad -> Hafsa -> Fanta. That's three steps.\n\nAlternatively, if we go through Aimee, she's connected to Seth, who is connected to Hafsa, who is connected to Fanta. So that's also three steps: Emery -> Aimee -> Seth -> Hafsa -> Fanta. Wait, that's four steps. Hmm, maybe I'm missing something.\n\nWait, let me check again. From Emery, go to Aimee, then Aimee is connected to Seth, who is connected to Hafsa, who is connected to Fanta. So that's three steps from Emery: Emery (0), Aimee (1), Seth (2), Hafsa (3), Fanta (4). But that's longer than the other path.\n\nAlternatively, from Emery, go to Eyad, who is connected to Hafsa, who is connected to Fanta. So that's two steps: Emery (0), Eyad (1), Hafsa (2), Fanta (3). Wait, that's three steps as well. Hmm, maybe I'm miscalculating.\n\nWait, maybe there's a shorter path. Let me see: Emery is connected to Eyad, who is connected to Hafsa, who is connected to Fanta. So that's three steps. Alternatively, Emery is connected to Aimee, who is connected to Seth, who is connected to Hafsa, who is connected to Fanta. That's four steps. So the shortest path is through Eyad, Hafsa, Fanta, which is three steps. \n\nWait, but maybe there's a direct connection I'm missing. Let me check the connections again. \n\nEmery is friends with Aimee and Eyad. Aimee is friends with Maimouna, Abdul, Seth, and Emery. Eyad is friends with Emery, Aimee, and Hafsa. Hafsa is friends with Eyad, Emery, Fanta, and Prince. So from Emery, going to Eyad, then Hafsa, then Fanta is the path. That's three steps. \n\nAlternatively, is there a way through Maimouna or Abdul? Let's see: Emery -> Aimee -> Maimouna -> Pedro -> ... but Pedro isn't connected to Fanta. Or Emery -> Aimee -> Abdul -> Pedro, but again, Pedro isn't connected to Fanta. So no, that path doesn't help.\n\nSo the shortest path is through Eyad, Hafsa, Fanta. That's three steps. Alternatively, is there a shorter path? Let me check again. \n\nWait, Hafsa is directly connected to Fanta, so from Eyad to Hafsa is one step, then Hafsa to Fanta is another. So from Emery to Eyad is one step, Eyad to Hafsa is two, Hafsa to Fanta is three. So the path is Emery -> Eyad -> Hafsa -> Fanta.\n\nAlternatively, if we go through Aimee, the path is longer. So the shortest path is through Eyad. Therefore, Emery should pass the message to Eyad first.\n</think>\n\neyad->hafsa->fanta eyad"  correct=eyad
