  [608/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Yitzchak should pass the message to Tessa or Santiago first to get it to Nahla as efficiently as possible. The question is about finding the shortest path in a friendship graph using BFS. \n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Yitzchak is friends with Tessa and Santiago. Let me see where each of them leads.\n\nLooking at Tessa, she's friends with Nahla and Yitzchak. So if Yitzchak sends the message to Tessa, Tessa can then pass it directly to Nahla. That's a two-step path: Yitzchak -> Tessa -> Nahla.\n\nNow, Santiago is friends with Yanki and Caitlin. Yanki is friends with Sheldon and Yitzchak. So if Yitzchak sends to Santiago, Santiago can pass to Yanki, then Yanki to Sheldon, then Sheldon to Nahla. That's a longer path: Yitzchak -> Santiago -> Yanki -> Sheldon -> Nahla.\n\nComparing both paths, the first option is shorter with only two steps. So Yitzchak should start with Tessa.\n</think>\n\ntessa -> nahla tessa"  correct=tessa
  [609/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Yitzchak should pass the message to Yanky or Tessa to get to Nahla the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll apply that here.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Yitzchak is friends with Yanky and Tessa. So from Yitzchak, the first step is Yanky and Tessa. Now, I need to see if either of them is connected to Nahla directly or through someone else.\n\nLooking at Yanky, he's friends with Sheldrick and Yitzchak. Sheldrick is also friends with Nahla. So Yank to Sheldrick to Nahla is a two-step path. That would make the path Yitzchak -> Yanky -> Sheldrick -> Nahla.\n\nNow, Tessa is friends with Nahla directly. So the path is Yitzchak -> Tessa -> Nahla, which is just two steps as well.\n\nWait, but BFS would explore all nodes at the same level before moving to the next. So from Yitzchak, both Yank and Tessa are at level 1. Tessa is directly connected to Nahla, so that's the shortest path with two steps. Yank's path goes through Sheldrick, which is another step, making it three steps in total.\n\nSo the shortest path is through Tessa, making the answer Tessa.\n</think>\n\nyitzchak -> tessa -> nahla  \ntessa"  correct=tessa
