  [614/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Tessa should pass the message to Yitzchak or Nahla to get to Sheldon the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll apply that here.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Tessa is friends with Yitzchak and Nahla. So from Tessa, the first step is to Yitzchak and Nahla. Now, I need to see which of these leads to Sheldon in fewer steps.\n\nLooking at Yitzchak's friends: he's connected to Santiago, Tessa, and Noor. Santiago is friends with Caflin, so that's another step. But wait, Caflin is friends with Sheldon. So from Yitzchak, it's Yitzchak -> Santiago -> Caflin -> Sheldon. That's three steps.\n\nNow for Nahla: she's friends with Tessa, Maria, and Sheldon. So directly from Nahla to Sheldon is one step. That's much quicker.\n\nSo the shortest path from Tessa to Sheldon is through Nahla, which is just one step. Therefore, Tessa should pass the message to Nahla.\n</think>\n\nnahla -> tessa  \nyitzchak  \n\nyitzchak"  correct=nahla
