tlin.\n\nIf we go through Yanki, Yanki is connected to Nahla, Sheldon, and Yitzchak. From Yanki, we can go to Yitzchak. Yitzchak is connected to Santiago, so that's two steps from Yanki, making it three steps from Nahla via Sheldon.\n\nAlternatively, from Sheldon, going to Maria. Maria is connected to Nahla, Sheldon, and Yanki. From Maria, we can go to Yanki, but that's already been visited. So, from Maria, we can't reach Santiago directly from here.\n\nFrom Sheldon, going to Caitlin. Caitlin is connected to Noor and Sheldon. From Caitlin, we can go to Noor. Noor is connected to Caitlin, Nusrat, and Faiga. From Noor, we can go to Nusrat or Faiga. Nusrat is connected to Yaakov and Xin. From Nusrat, we can go to Yaakov. Yaakov is connected to Faiga and Nusrat. From Yaakov, we can go to Faiga. Faiga is connected to Noor and Yaakov. This path seems longer.\n\nAlternatively, from Caitlin, going to Noor. Noor is connected to Nusrat and Faiga. From Noor, we can go to Nusrat. Nusrat is connected to Yaakov and Xin. From Nusrat, we can go to Yaakov. Yaakov is connected to Faiga. From Faiga, we can go to Noor, which is already visited. This path doesn't lead to Santiago.\n\nSo, the path through Sheldon seems to take more steps.\n\nNow, let's consider the path through Tessa. Tessa is connected to Nahla and Yitzchak. From Tessa, we can go to Yitzchak. Yitzchak is connected to Santiago, Yanki, and Tessa. So, from Yitzchak, we can go directly to Santiago. That's two steps from Tessa, making it three steps from Nahla via Tessa.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's a shorter path. From Tessa, Yitzchak, then Santiago. That's two steps from Tessa, so three steps from Nahla.\n\nAlternatively, from Tessa, Yitzchak, Santiago. That's the shortest path.\n\nComparing the two paths:\n\n- Through Sheldon: Nahla -> Sheldon -> Yanki -> Yitzchak -> Santiago. That's four steps.\n\n- Through Tessa: Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak -> Santiago. That's three steps.\n\nWait, but I think I made a mistake earlier. Let me recount.\n\nFrom Nahla, go to Tessa. From Tessa, go to Yitzchak. From Yitzchak, go to Santiago. So, that's three steps: Nahla (0), Tessa (1), Yitzchak (2), Santiago (3). So, the path is Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak -> Santiago.\n\nAlternatively, through Sheldon: Nahla -> Sheldon -> Yanki -> Yitzchak -> Santiago. That's four steps.\n\nSo, the shortest path is through Tessa, taking three steps.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's a shorter path through another route. For example, from Nahla to Maria, then Maria to Yanki, then Yanki to Yitzchak, then Yitzchak to Santiago. That's four steps as well.\n\nAlternatively, from Nahla to Yanki, then Yanki to Yitzchak, then Yitzchak to Santiago. That's three steps: Nahla -> Yanki -> Yitzchak -> Santiago.\n\nWait, that's three steps as well. So, the path through Yanki is also three steps.\n\nSo, the shortest path is three steps, either through Tessa or through Yanki.\n\nBut the question is whether Nahla should pass to Sheldon or Tessa first. So, the options are between Sheldon and Tessa.\n\nFrom the BFS, the shortest path is through Tessa, so she should pass to Tessa first.\n\nWait, but let me confirm. The BFS would explore all nodes at distance 1, then distance 2, etc.\n\nStarting from Nahla, distance 0.\n\nHer friends: Sheldon, Maria, Tessa, Yanki. Distance 1.\n\nFrom each of these, we explore their friends, excluding Nahla.\n\nFrom Sheldon: friends are Yanki, Maria, Caitlin. Yanki and Maria are already at distance 1, so Caitlin is at distance 2.\n\nFrom Maria: friends are Nahla, Sheldon, Yanki. All already visited.\n\nFrom Tessa: friends are Yitzchak. Yitzchak is at distance 2.\n\nFrom Yanki: friends are Nahla, Sheldon, Yitzchak. Yitzchak is at distance 2.\n\nFrom Caitlin: friends are Noor and Sheldon. Noor is at distance 2.\n\nFrom Noor: friends are Caitlin, Nusrat, Faiga. Nusrat and Faiga are at distance 3.\n\nFrom Yitzchak: friends are Santiago, Yanki, Tessa. Santiago is at distance 3.\n\nSo, the shortest path