  [664/1150] "<think>\nAlright, let's tackle this problem step by step. So, the question is about determining whether Caitlin should pass a message to Santiago or Xin first to reach Sheldon the fastest. We need to use BFS for this.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the friendships to visualize the graph. Let's list out all the connections:\n\n- Nahla is friends with Sheldon, Maria, and Tessa.\n- Sheldon is friends with Nahla, Maria, Yanki, and Caitlin.\n- Maria is friends with Nahla, Sheldon, and Caitlin.\n- Caitlin is friends with Maria, Sheldon, and Santiago.\n- Santiago is friends with Yanki and Caitlin.\n- Yanki is friends with Santiago, Nahla, and Yitzchak.\n- Yitzchak is friends with Yanki, Tessa, and Faiga.\n- Tessa is friends with Yitzchak and Nahla.\n- Faiga is friends with Yitzchak and Noor.\n- Noor is friends with Faiga, Caitlin, and Xin.\n- XIN is friends with Noor and Caitlin.\n- Yitzchak is also friends with Santiago.\n\nWait, I think I might have missed some connections. Let me double-check:\n\nLooking back, the connections are:\n\n- Yitzchak is friends with Santiago.\n- Noor is friends with XIN and Caitlin.\n- XIN is friends with Noor and Caitlin.\n- Yitzchak is friends with Faiga and Noor.\n- Noor is friends with Faiga, C, and XIN.\n- Caitlin is friends with Maria, Sheldon, Santiago, and XIN.\n\nSo, starting from Caitlin, we need to find the shortest path to Sheldon.\n\nBFS starts at Caitlin. The first level is Caitlin's friends: Maria, Santiago, XIN.\n\nNow, check if any of these are Sheldon. Maria is connected to Sheldon, so the path is Caitlin -> Maria -> Sheldon. That's two steps.\n\nBut wait, is there a shorter path? Let's see. Caitlin can go to XIN, but XIN is connected to Noor, who is connected to Faiga, Yitzchak, and Caitlin. Yitzchak is connected to Santiago and Faiga, and Santiago is connected to Yanki. Yanki is connected to Nahla, who is connected to Sheldon. So that path would be longer.\n\nAlternatively, Caitlin to Maria to Sheldon is two steps. S