  [669/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether XIN should pass the message to CAITLIN or NUSRAT first to get to YANKY the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll apply that here.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. XIN is friends with CAITLIN and NUSRAT. CAITLIN is connected to XIN, SANTIAGO, and YANKY. NUSRAT is connected to XIN, NOOR, and YUSIF (I think that's the name). NOOR is friends with XIN, NUSRAT, and CAITLIN. YANKY is connected to YITZCHAK and YANKY? Wait, no, YANKY is connected to YITZCHAK and maybe others. Let me check the data.\n\nLooking at the friendships, YANKY is friends with YITZCHAK. YITZCHAK is friends with YANKY, TESSEL, and Santiago. Santiago is friends with YankY and Caitlin. So from XIN, if I go to CAITLIN, she can reach YankY directly. That's one step.\n\nAlternatively, if XIN goes to NUSRAT, Nusrat is friends with NOOR and YUSIF. NOOR is friends with XIN, Nusrat, and CAITLIN. So from Nusrat, NOOR can go to CAITLIN, who can then reach YankY. That's two steps: XIN -> Nusrat -> NOOR -> Caitlin -> YankY. Wait, no, that's more steps. Alternatively, Nusrat is friends with YUSIF, but I don't see YankY connected to YUSIF. So maybe that path isn't direct.\n\nWait, maybe I'm missing something. Let me list the connections again.\n\nXIN is friends with CAITLIN and NUSRAT.\n\nCaitlin is friends with XIN, SANTIAGO, and YANKY.\n\nSo from XIN to Caitlin is one step, and Caitlin can reach YankY in another step. So the path would be XIN -> Caitlin -> YankY, which is two steps.\n\nAlternatively, XIN -> Nusrat. Nusrat is friends with XIN, NOOR, and YUSIF. NOOR is friends with XIN, Nusrat, and Caitlin. So from Nusrat, NOOR can go to Caitlin, who can then reach YankY. So that's XIN -> Nusrat -> NOOR -> Caitlin -> YankY, which is three steps.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path. Let me check if YankY is directly connected to anyone else. YankY is friends with YITZCHAK. YITZCHAK 