  [683/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Tessa should pass the message to Nahla or Yitzchak to get it to Xin the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll use that approach.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Tessa is friends with Yitzchak and Nahla. So from Tessa, the first step is either Yitzchak or Nahla.\n\nLooking at Yitzchak's friends: He's connected to Santiago, Tessa, Noor, and Faiga. Noor is friends with Xin, Caitlin, and Nusrat. Nusrat is friends with Xin and Yaakov. Yaakov is friends with Faiga. So from Yitzchak, it's two steps to reach Xin through Noor or Nusrat.\n\nNow, looking at Nahla's friends: She's connected to Tessa, Sheldon, Maria, and Yanki. Sheldon is friends with Maria, Yanki, and Nahla. Yanki is friends with Sheldon and Yitzchak. So from Nahla, it's also two steps to reach Xin through Maria or Yanki.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path. Let me check again. From Tessa to Nahla is one step. From Nahla to Maria is two steps. From Maria to Sheldon is three steps. From Sheldon to Yanki is four steps. From Yanki to Yitzchak is five steps. From Yitzchak to Noor is six steps. From Noor to Xin is seven steps. That's a long path.\n\nAlternatively, from Tessa to Yitzchak is one step. From Yitzchak to Noor is two steps. From Noor to Xin is three steps. That's shorter.\n\nSo the shortest path from Tessa to Xin is through Yitzchak, making it three steps. Therefore, Tessa should pass the message to Yitzchak first.\n</think>\n\ntessa -> yitzchak -> noor -> xin\n\nyitzchak"  correct=yitzchak
  [684/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Tessa should pass the message to Nahla or Yitzchak to get it to Noor the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll apply that here.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Tessa is friends with Yitzchak and Nahla. Yitzchak is connected to Santiago, Tessa, and Noor. Nahla is connected to Tessa, Maria, and Sheldon. Maria is connected to Nahla and Sheldon, and Sheldon is connected to Maria, Yanki, and Tessa. Yanki is friends with Sheldon and Yitzchak. So from Tessa, the first step is either Yitzchak or Nahla.\n\nLooking at Yitzchak, he's connected to Santiago and Noor. So if Tessa sends to Yitzchak, the next step is to Noor. That's two steps: Tessa -> Yitzchak -> Noor.\n\nIf Tessa sends to Nahla, Nahla is connected to Maria and Sheldon. Maria is connected to Sheldon, and Sheldon is connected to Nahla and Yanki. Yanki is connected to Yitzchak. So from Nahla, to get to Noor, we'd have to go through Maria to Sheldon, then to Yanki, then to Yitzchak, and then to Noor. That's five steps, which is longer.\n\nSo the shortest path is Tessa -> Yitzchak -> Noor.\n</think>\n\ntessa -> yitzchak -> noor\nyitzchak"  correct=yitzchak
