  [747/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Jaliyah should pass the message to Mackenzie or Bruno first to get to Cesar the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll use that approach.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the connections. Jaliyah is friends with Bruno and Mackenzie. Bruno is connected to Luc, Eunice, and Jaliyah. M is connected to J, D, and L. Let's see how each path from Jaliyah to Cesar unfolds.\n\nStarting with the direct friends:\n- If Jaliyah goes to Bruno (B), Bruno is connected to Eunice, Luc, and Jaliyah. From Bruno, Eunice is friends with A and C. So, B->E->C is a path of length 2.\n- If Jaliyah goes to M (M), M is connected to J, D, and L. From M, D is connected to A and M. A is connected to C and D. So, M->D->A->C is a path of length 3.\n\nComparing the two, the path through Bruno is shorter. So, the shortest path is Jaliyah -> Bruno -> Eunice -> Cesar, which is 3 steps. Therefore, Jaliyah should start with Bruno.\n</think>\n\njaliyah -> bruno -> eunice -> cesar  \nbruno"  correct=mackenzie
