ry to visualize it.\n\nJaliyah's friends are Bruno and Mack. So, the first step is to check both Bruno and Mack.\n\nFrom Bruno, he's connected to Jali, Luc, and Abdu. From each of those, I can go further.\n\nFrom Mack, he's connected to Jali, Legend, and Derk.\n\nI need to see which path reaches Alyssa faster.\n\nAlyssa is connected to Euni, Ces, and Derk.\n\nSo, starting from Bruno:\n\nBruno -> Jali -> Alys? Wait, no, Alys is connected to Euni, Ces, and Derk. So from Bruno, we go to Jali, then to Alys. That's two steps.\n\nFrom Mack:\n\nMack -> Legend -> Ces -> Euni -> Alys. That's four steps.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path. Let me check again.\n\nFrom Bruno: Bruno -> Jali -> Alys. That's two steps.\n\nFrom Mack: Mack -> Legend -> Ces -> Euni -> Alys. Four steps.\n\nSo the shortest path is through Bruno, taking two steps.\n\nWait, but maybe there's another way. Let me check if Alys is directly connected to anyone else.\n\nAlyssa is connected to Euni, Ces, and Derk. So from Alys, you can't go further unless you have more connections, but in the given data, Alys is only connected to Euni, Ces, and Derk.\n\nSo, the path through Bruno is shorter. Therefore, Jaliyah should pass the message to Bruno first.\n</think>\n\nthe shortest path is jaliyah -> bruno -> abdu -> jor -> alyssa. the correct option is bruno.\n\nbruno"  correct=mackenzie
