steps. So the shortest path is through Malak, which is two steps.\n\nWait, but I'm confused because earlier I thought both were three steps. Maybe I was wrong about Malak. Let me check again.\n\nYes, Malak is directly connected to Quin. So the path is Cameron -> Malak -> Quin. That's two steps. So the shortest path is through Malak.\n\nWait, but in the initial BFS, I thought both were three steps. Maybe I was mistaken. Let me clarify.\n\nCameron's friends: Isiah, Malak.\n\nFrom Isiah: friends are Ayden, Cam, and Quin? Wait, no, Ayden is friends with Isiah, but Isiah's friends are Ayden, Cam, and Quin? Wait, looking back, the data says: esmeralda is friends with quinn, quinn is friends with esmeralda, and quinn is friends with ayden. So Isiah is friends with Ayden and Cam. So Isiah's friends are Ayden and Cam. So from Isiah, you can go to Ayden, who is friends with Quin. So Cameron -> Isiah -> Ayden -> Quin: three steps.\n\nFrom Malak: friends are Ayden, Quin, Sima. So from Malak, you can go directly to Quin. So Cameron -> Malak -> Quin: two steps.\n\nSo the shortest path is through Malak, which is two steps. Therefore, Cameron should pass the message to Malak first.\n</think>\n\nmalak quin\n\nmalak"  correct=malak
