, M.\n- F is friends with S and maybe others.\n\nWait, I think I\'m mixing up the names. Let me list each person and their friends:\n\n1. Joziah (J) friends: K\n2. K friends: J, E, M\n3. E friends: K, S\n4. S friends: E, M, F\n5. M friends: S, Q, C\n6. Q friends: M, E\n7. C friends: M, I\n8. I friends: C, A\n9. A friends: I, Q, E\n10. F friends: S\n11. Quin (Q) friends: M, E\n12. Sima (S) friends: E, M, F\n13. Esmeralda (E) friends: K, S, A, M\n14. Magaly (M) friends: K, E, F\n15. Malak (M) friends: S, Q, C\n16. Isiah (I) friends: C, A\n17. Ayden (A) friends: I, Q, E\n18. Cam (C) friends: M, I\n19. Esteban (E) friends: K, S, A\n20. Sima (S) friends: E, M, F\n21. Quin (Q) friends: M, E\n22. Malak (M) friends: S, Q, C\n23. Franscua (F) friends: S, maybe others.\n\nWait, I think I\'m getting tangled up. Let me try to build the graph step by step.\n\nStarting with K (Kendra):\n\n- K is friends with J, E, M.\n\nSo K\'s friends are J, E, M.\n\nNow, for each of these, we can explore their friends:\n\nFrom J: J is friends with K. No new nodes.\n\nFrom E: E is friends with K, S. So S is added.\n\nFrom M: M is friends with S, Q, C.\n\nSo now, the next layer is S, Q, C.\n\nNow, from S: S is friends with E, M, F. E and M are already visited, so F is added.\n\nFrom Q: Q is friends with M, E. Both already visited.\n\nFrom C: C is friends with M, I. M is visited, so I is added.\n\nNow, the next layer is F, I.\n\nFrom F: F is friends with S, maybe others. S is visited.\n\nFrom I: I is friends with C, A. C is visited, so A is added.\n\nNow, the next layer is A.\n\nFrom A: A is friends with I, Q, E. All visited.\n\nSo the BFS tree from K is:\n\nLevel 0: K\n\nLevel 1: J, E, M\n\nLevel 2: S, Q, C\n\nLevel 3: F, I\n\nLevel 4: A\n\nSo the shortest path from K to M is through E or M directly. Wait, M is at level 1, so the distance is 1. But wait, M is a friend of K, so the distance is 1. But the question is about reaching Malcolm, not M. Wait, the question is about reaching Malcolm, whose