aly." So the path is Quinna -> Esmeralda -> Magaly -> Kendra. That\'s three steps.\n\nAlternatively, from Quinna to Malak, then to Ayden, then to Isiah, then to Cameron, then to Kendra. That\'s five steps, which is longer.\n\nSo the shortest path from Quinna to Kendra is through Esmeralda, then Magaly, then Kendra. That\'s three steps, which is shorter than going through Malak, which would take four steps.\n\nWait, but does Malak connect to anyone else who can reach Kendra faster? Let me check. Malak is connected to Quinna, Ayden, Sima, and Cameron. Ayden connects to Isiah, who connects to Kendra. So from Malak to Isiah to Kendra is three steps: Malak -> Ayden -> Isiah -> Kendra. Wait, that\'s three steps as well.\n\nWait, but from Quinna to Malak, then to Ayden, then to Isiah, then to Kendra. That\'s four steps. But from Quinna to Esmeralda, then to Magaly, then to Kendra is three steps. So the shortest path is through Esmeralda.\n\nWait, but I\'m getting confused. Let me list all possible paths:\n\nFrom Quinna:\n- To Esmeralda: step 1\n  - From Esmeralda: to Magaly (step 2)\n    - From Magaly: to Kendra (step 3)\n- To Malak: step 1\n  - From Malak: to Ayden (step 2)\n    - From Ayden: to Isiah (step 3)\n      - From Isiah: to Kendra (step 4)\n\nSo the path through Esmeralda is shorter, taking three steps, while through Malak takes four steps. Therefore, Quinna should pass the message to Esmeralda first.\n</think>\n\nesmeralda Kendra'  correct=esmeralda
