  [1028/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Joziah should pass the message to Malcolm or Kendra to get to Quinn the fastest. I remember that BFS is used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph, so I'll use that approach.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the friendships to build the graph. Let me list out all the connections:\n\n- Joziah is friends with Kendra and Malcom (from the given data).\n- Kendra is friends with Joziah, Malcom, and Magaly.\n- Malcom is friends with Joziah, Kendra, and Magaly.\n- Magaly is friends with Kendra and Malcom.\n- So, Joziah is directly connected to both Malcolm and Kendra. Since both are at distance 1 from Joziah, either could be the first step. But since we're using BFS, both paths are equally short. However, the question is about efficiency, so either choice would result in the message reaching Quinn in the same number of steps. Therefore, it doesn't matter which one Joziah chooses first. The shortest path would be either Joziah -> Malcolm or Joziah -> Kendra, both leading to Quinn in the next steps.\n</think>\n\nThe shortest path from Joziah to Quinn is either through Malcolm or Kendra. Since both are at the same distance, either choice is equally efficient. \n\nmalcolm kendra"  correct=kendra
