nd Jayceon. So from Tessa, we can't reach Mya. Therefore, the path through Harlow doesn't reach Mya, but the path through Yechezkel does.\n\nWait, but the question is about the shortest path. So perhaps the path through Yechezkel is shorter.\n\nWait, but let me think again. From Jayceon, if I go to Harlow, then to Claudia, then to Frey, then to Tessa, but Tessa doesn't connect to Mya. So that path doesn't reach Mya. Therefore, the only way is through Yechezkel.\n\nWait, but maybe there's another path through Harlow. Let me see: Jayceon -> Harlow -> Claudia -> Frey -> Tessa -> ... but again, no Mya. Alternatively, from Claudia, go to Freddy -> Raymond, but that's not helpful. Alternatively, from Claudia, go to Frey -> Tessa -> Mya? No, Tessa isn't connected to Mya.\n\nWait, perhaps I'm missing a connection. Let me check Mya's connections again. Mya is connected to Ruth, Aidan, and Vihaan. So from Mya, you can go to Ruth, Aidan, or Vihaan. But in the BFS, we're starting from Jayceon and trying to reach Mya. So perhaps the path through Harlow is longer.\n\nWait, maybe I'm overcomplicating this. Let me try to perform BFS manually.\n\nStarting from Jayceon, level 0: Jayceon.\n\nLevel 1: Yechezkel, Harlow, Tessa.\n\nFrom Yechezkel, level 2: Journey.\n\nFrom Harlow, level 2: Claudia.\n\nFrom Tessa, level 2: Frey.\n\nNow, from Journey (level 2), connected to Vihaan.\n\nFrom Claudia (level 2), connected to Frey, Freddy.\n\nFrom Frey (level 2), connected to Tessa.\n\nFrom Vihaan (level 3), connected to Mya.\n\nSo the path through Yechezkel is Jayceon -> Yechezkel -> Journey -> Vihaan -> Mya, which is 4 steps.\n\nThe path through Harlow is Jayceon -> Harlow -> Claudia -> Frey -> Tessa, but Tessa doesn't connect to Mya. Alternatively, from Claudia, go to Freddy -> Raymond, but that's not helpful. Alternatively, from Claudia, go to Frey -> Tessa -> ... but no Mya.\n\nWait, but Mya is connected to Vihaan, who is connected to Ruth, who is connected to Journey, who is connected to 